,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":34.500557324,"data":"Conclusion:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":34.500587396,"data":"  Yes -- mood improves after watching cat videos. The positive-emotion\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":34.500592547,"data":"  composite rose +0.77 points (3.99 -\u003e 4.76) and the negative-\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":34.500597842,"data":"  emotion composite fell 0.74 points (2.19 -\u003e 1.46); both\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":34.500602,"data":"  nulls are rejected with t ~ 50-60 (df ~ 6,600), sign-flip p \u003c 1e-5, and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":34.500606548,"data":"  bootstrap CIs far from 0. Happiest single emotion: +1.14\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":34.500610317,"data":"  (4.08 -\u003e 5.22); viewers also felt more energetic (+0.51)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":34.500614292,"data":"  and less depleted, anxious, annoyed, sad and guilty (all |t| \u003e= 26.7,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":34.500635708,"data":"  p \u003c .001). Caveats: retrospective self-report, no control group, and a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":34.500638834,"data":"  self-selected snowball sample (88.4% female) -- so 'improves mood' is\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":34.50064125,"data":"  supported as a within-person association around real viewing episodes,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":34.500643774,"data":"  not as a causal effect of an assigned treatment.\n"}
